@page "/"

<div class="hero-section">
    <h1 class="page-title">V-Drum Explorer</h1>
    <p class="page-subtitle">Explore and edit Roland V-Drum settings from your browser</p>
</div>

<div class="card-modern">
    <h2 class="card-title">MIDI Device Demo</h2>
    <p class="card-text">
        This page demonstrates using <a href="https://blazor.net">Blazor</a> to run C# code in the
        browser, interacting with the <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/webmidi/#listing-inputs-and-outputs">Web MIDI API</a>
        to list information about selected Roland instruments. (Currently supported: the V-Drums TD-17, TD-27 and TD-50; the Aerophone AE-10.)
    </p>
    <div class="info-links">
        <a href="https://jskeet.github.io/DemoCode/Drums" class="info-link">Documentation</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/jskeet/DemoCode/tree/master/Drums" class="info-link">Source Code</a>
        <a href="https://codeblog.jonskeet.uk/category/v-drums/" class="info-link">Blog Posts</a>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card-modern">
    <h3 class="card-title">Getting Started</h3>
    <p class="card-text">
        When you click the "List kits" button below, you may need to accept a request to use your local MIDI devices,
        as the page requires access to make System Exclusive requests.
    </p>
    <p class="card-text">
        The code is expected to work on Chrome and Chromium-based Edge. It may not work in Safari or Firefox.
    </p>
    <p class="card-text">
        Note: the code will give up if it detects multiple supported Roland devices (or none). If you change which devices
        are connected, just reload the page and press the button again.
    </p>
    <button class="btn-modern btn-primary-modern" @onclick="ListKits">List kits</button>
</div>

<div class="status-grid">
    <div class="info-card">
        <div class="info-card-label">MIDI Status</div>
        <div class="info-card-value">@status</div>
    </div>
    <div class="info-card">
        <div class="info-card-label">Input Ports</div>
        <div class="info-card-value">@inputDevices</div>
    </div>
    <div class="info-card">
        <div class="info-card-label">Output Ports</div>
        <div class="info-card-value">@outputDevices</div>
    </div>
</div>

@if (messages.Any())
{
    <div class="log-panel">
        <div class="log-header">Log</div>
        <div class="log-content">
            @foreach (var message in messages)
            {
                <div class="log-entry">@message</div>
            }
        </div>
    </div>
}
